sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Credit: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1842-2028) now returns 16 reference-anchored measurements; the 7 new ones (L1863-1934) report a non-trivial FEM result (max lamella 2.78 um against the geometric arrest bound a_0/sqrt(6) = 6.04 um; twinned-area ratio 0.123 against the phi = 0.50 null; k ratio 0.193) and the templating result (IoU 0.753 against 1.0 with the 0.418 flux-matched control in the method string). Deductions: the headline Pass 2 validation — 12-species r = 0.9997 (L1938-1947) — is circular because the table's e_rel_obs equals e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 by construction (-5); the Gibson-Ashby 2.0x at phi = 0.5 (L1988-1997) is the algebraic identity C phi/(C phi^2), chi = -4 (L1978-1987) is a lookup (L446-453) not computed from the field, and Z = 0 (L1998-2007) is assigned via get_tpms_nodal_strut_vectors(\"none\") (L441) (-3); several Pass 3 references are weak: the stiffness ratio reference 0.19 is Gibson-Ashby stretching although the 2D honeycomb is bending-dominated (L1895-1903), the pore-arrest fraction 0.26 vs ideal 1.0 includes notch-singularity elements at hexagon vertices (L1885-1893), the largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 against a reference of 1.0 (the single chance primary-nucleation event at k_1 = 1e-7 seeds a second domain holding 23% of the crystalline pixels; the self-test's `domains <= 2` does not catch this and the Phase A handoff reported it as ~0.999) (L1915-1923), and the ACC-fraction reference 0.0 is asymptotic rather than a literature time point (L1925-1934) (-3); the specimen a_0 reference is self-referential (L2018-2027) (-1). Net -6 from v2." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json L86–L98: DEFECT: cross_taxa_echinoderm_stereom_table has no per-row figure/table/DOI provenance; TPMS-type assignments (e.g. Cidaris rugosa 'Primitive P') unsupported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json#L86-L98>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1885–L1903: Pass 3 references of limited strength: pore-arrest ideal 1.0 vs 0.26 (notch-vertex twinning), stiffness ratio reference 0.19 = stretching C phi while the honeycomb section is bending-dominated (GA 2.3 (t/l)^3 = 0.288 noted in the source string) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1885-L1903>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1915–L1923: DEFECT: largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 (measurements.yaml) vs reference 1.0 — a chance primary event seeds a 23% second domain; the self-test's domains <= 2 (L2130) does not catch it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1915-L1923>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1938–L1947: DEFECT: 12-species Pearson r = 0.9997 is circular — reference-table e_rel_obs is e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 for every row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1938-L1947>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1978–L2007: DEFECT: chi = -4 is a genus lookup (L446-453), 2.0x Gibson-Ashby ratio is the identity C phi/(C phi^2), pinch-off Z = 0 is assigned via the 'none' strut set (L441) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1978-L2007>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-3d-schwarz-diamond-tpms-implicit-surface-mean-curvature-h-on-zero-level-set>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-3d-schwarz-diamond-tpms-zero-level-set-solid-volume-fraction-phi-c-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-acc-fraction-of-spicule-mineral-remaining-after-48-h-of-templated-secondary-nucleation-transformation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-crinoid-ossicle-sem-specimen-segmented-solid-calcite-volume-fraction-crinoid-stereom-ossicle-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-crinoid-ossicle-sem-specimen-segmented-trabecular-lattice-period-a-0-crinoid-stereom-ossicle-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-elastic-flat-punch-indentation-stiffness-ratio-of-the-111-diamond-lattice-section-to-the-monolithic-single-crystal>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-gibson-ashby-stretching-tpms-phi-1-vs-bending-foam-phi-2-stiffness-amplification-at-phi-0-50>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-largest-crystallographic-domain-fraction-of-spicule-calcite-under-secondary-nucleation-dominated-acc-calcite-transformation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-fraction-of-lattice-twinned-elements-adjacent-to-a-strut-pore-interface-free-surface-arrest>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-twin-band-max-lamella-run-length-in-the-111-diamond-lattice-section-at-4x-monolith-twin-onset-depth>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-twinned-area-confinement-ratio-lattice-monolith-at-equal-indentation-depth-4x-onset>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-schwarz-diamond-z-4-tetrahedral-inter-strut-angle-arccos-1-3-in-protoreaster-nodosus>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-super-threshold-pinch-off-ablation-negative-control-nodal-strut-valence-c-1-35>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-syncytial-membrane-templating-fidelity-iou-mineral-tpms-template-after-48-h-of-acc-vesicle-delivery>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-tpms-unit-cell-euler-characteristic-chi-2-2g-for-genus-g-3-bicontinuous-stereom>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation-2> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "12-species Echinodermata TPMS vs labyrinthic stereom relative modulus correlation E*/E_s = 0.9997 Pearson r" ;
        dcterms:description "TPMS mean E*/E_s = 0.1750 vs labyrinthic mean = 0.0647" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Correlation of Gibson-Ashby stretching (phi^1) and bending (phi^2) relative modulus predictions against observed stereom stiffness across 12 Asteroidea, Crinoidea, Echinoidea, and Ophiuroidea species (RMSE=0.0013)" ;
        schema:name "12-species Echinodermata TPMS vs labyrinthic stereom relative modulus correlation E*/E_s" ;
        schema:unitText "Pearson r" ;
        schema:value "0.9997" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s-reference> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dcterms:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652 & Gibson & Ashby (1997) Cellular Solids" ;
        schema:value "1.0" .

